net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: scope DSA port queues to the MediaTek tag

mtk_select_queue() sends a DSA conduit's frames through queue
skb_get_queue_mapping() + 3, and mtk_device_event() rate-limits queue
dp->index + 3 to that user port's link speed. Only the MediaTek tagger
sets the queue mapping to the port index, so the scheme is sound only for
MediaTek-tagged switches; the QDMA queues are shared by all MACs.

On a SoC that also carries a switch with another tagger (BPI-R4 Pro:
MxL862xx behind its own GMAC), that conduit's frames all leave with
queue mapping 0, land in queue 3 and inherit the link rate of MediaTek
switch port 0, incorrectly limiting egress to an unrelated port's speed.
The other tagger's port speeds also reprogram queues owned by MediaTek
switch ports.

Use the per-port queues, and their rate limits, only for conduits whose
tag protocol is DSA_TAG_PROTO_MTK. Any other conduit transmits on its MAC
queue like a non-DSA port.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3748,6 +3748,13 @@
 	if (!dsa_user_dev_check(dev))
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
+	/* Only MediaTek-tagged conduits map a user port to queue index + 3
+	 * (see mtk_select_queue). Ports behind another tag share no such
+	 * mapping, so their speed must not reprogram another port's queue.
+	 */
+	if (!mtk_uses_dsa(ldev))
+		return NOTIFY_DONE;
+
 	if (__ethtool_get_link_ksettings(dev, &s))
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
@@ -5059,7 +5066,13 @@
 	struct mtk_mac *mac = netdev_priv(dev);
 	unsigned int queue = 0;
 
-	if (netdev_uses_dsa(dev))
+	/* Queue index + 3 is the per-port queue that mtk_device_event()
+	 * rate-limits to the port's link speed, and only the MediaTek tagger
+	 * sets that index. A conduit for another tagger would otherwise send
+	 * every frame through queue 3 and inherit the speed of MediaTek switch
+	 * port 0 (BPI-R4 Pro: all MxL862xx ports capped at lan1's link rate).
+	 */
+	if (mtk_uses_dsa(dev))
 		queue = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) + 3;
 	else
 		queue = mac->id;
